    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45-a2">

                <pb facs="0110" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg60"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 225.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Senhor Nascimento.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge your excellency’s communication of March 14,
                    declaring that the revolt in the port of the federal capital is at an end, and
                    of the determination on the part of the Government to maintain the free
                    operation of commerce. I have the honor further to tender congratulations to his
                    excellency the Sr. marechal vice-president of the Republic, upon the successful
                    termination of the issue which has enabled the Government to give this
                    assurance.</p>
                <p>I improve, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. L.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
